  "answer": "This has been reported before. The crash is a PowerToys Run (PTRun) COMException 0x80263001, 'Desktop composition is disabled'. It comes from the Windows desktop compositor (DWM) resetting, which is what blacks out the screens. PowerToys then shows the error dialog. The root cause varies by machine. It is often a graphics driver reset or update, or memory exhaustion, and is usually outside PowerToys. The tracking ticket, PowerToys#31226, gives the fix: update PowerToys to 0.96 or newer, where PowerToys Run handles this more gracefully. You are on 0.86.0. Update to the latest version. Also keep your GPU drivers and Windows up to date. Related tickets (#42549, #43125) were closed as duplicates of #31226."
 },
